James Rising received a request from Mfah Amadu expressing his interest in a PhD program at the University of Delaware, focusing on Environmental Economics. Mfah detailed his educational background, including an MSc in Climate Change and Sustainable Development and a research interest in the carbon credit market for climate finance in developing countries. James drafted a professional response indicating that he would not be taking on new PhD students for Fall 2026 and encouraged Mfah to explore other faculty options. The direct and concise exchange reflects the academic mentorship process while maintaining professionalism.
